          <Strong>PART 2</Strong>
        </Number><Title>Qualifying young persons: prescribed conditions</Title><P1group RestrictStartDate="2025-09-01" RestrictExtent="E+W+S+N.I."><Title>Education and training condition</Title><P1 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2006/223/regulation/3" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2006/223/regulation/3" id="regulation-3"><Pnumber>3</Pnumber><P1para><P2 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2006/223/regulation/3/1" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2006/223/regulation/3/1" id="regulation-3-1"><Pnumber>1</Pnumber><P2para><Text>This regulation applies in the case of a person who has not attained the age of 20.</Text></P2para></P2><P2 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2006/223/regulation/3/2" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2006/223/regulation/3/2" id="regulation-3-2"><Pnumber>2</Pnumber><P2para><Text>The condition is that the person—</Text><P3 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2006/223/regulation/3/2/a" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2006/223/regulation/3/2/a" id="regulation-3-2-a"><Pnumber>a</Pnumber><P3para><Text>is undertaking a course of full-time education, which is not advanced education and which is not provided by virtue of his employment or any office held by him—</Text><P4 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2006/223/regulation/3/2/a/i" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2006/223/regulation/3/2/a/i" id="regulation-3-2-a-i"><Pnumber><CommentaryRef Ref="key-a1"/>i</Pnumber><P4para><Text>. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .</Text></P4para></P4><P4 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2006/223/regulation/3/2/a/ii" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2006/223/regulation/3/2/a/ii" id="regulation-3-2-a-ii"><Pnumber><CommentaryRef Ref="key-a1"/>ii</Pnumber><P4para><Text>. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .</Text></P4para></P4></P3para></P3><P3 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2006/223/regulation/3/2/ab" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2006/223/regulation/3/2/ab" id="regulation-3-2-ab"><Pnumber><CommentaryRef Ref="key-a2"/>ab</Pnumber><P3para><Text>. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .</Text></P3para></P3><P3 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2006/223/regulation/3/2/b" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2006/223/regulation/3/2/b" id="regulation-3-2-b"><Pnumber>b</Pnumber><P3para><Text>having undertaken such a course as is mentioned in  <Substitution ChangeId="key-a3" CommentaryRef="key-a3">paragraph (a) </Substitution><CommentaryRef Ref="key-a4"/><Substitution ChangeId="key-a3" CommentaryRef="key-a3">...</Substitution>   <Substitution ChangeId="key-a5" CommentaryRef="key-a5">has been accepted or is enrolled to undertake a further such course;</Substitution></Text></P3para></P3><P3 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2006/223/regulation/3/2/c" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2006/223/regulation/3/2/c" id="regulation-3-2-c"><Pnumber>c</Pnumber><P3para><Text>is undertaking approved training that is not provided by means of a contract of employment<Addition ChangeId="key-a6" CommentaryRef="key-a6">; or</Addition></Text></P3para></P3></P2para></P2><P3 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2006/223/regulation/3/d" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2006/223/regulation/3/d" id="regulation-3-d"><Pnumber><Addition ChangeId="key-a6" CommentaryRef="key-a6">d</Addition></Pnumber><P3para><Text><Addition ChangeId="key-a6" CommentaryRef="key-a6">having undertaken a course mentioned in paragraph (a) or approved training mentioned in paragraph (c), has been accepted or is enrolled to undertake such approved training</Addition>.</Text></P3para></P3><P2 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2006/223/regulation/3/3" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2006/223/regulation/3/3" id="regulation-3-3"><Pnumber><CommentaryRef Ref="key-a7"/>3</Pnumber><P2para><Text>. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .</Text></P2para></P2><P2 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2006/223/regulation/3/4" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2006/223/regulation/3/4" id="regulation-3-4"><Pnumber>4</Pnumber><P2para><Text>A person who is aged 19 is only a qualifying young person by virtue of  <Substitution ChangeId="key-a8" CommentaryRef="key-a8">paragraph (2)(a)</Substitution><CommentaryRef Ref="key-a9"/><Substitution ChangeId="key-a8" CommentaryRef="key-a8">...</Substitution>  or (2)(c) if he began the education or training (as the case may be) referred to in that sub-paragraph<Addition ChangeId="key-a10" CommentaryRef="key-a10">, or was accepted or enrolled to undertake that education or training,</Addition>  before attaining that age.</Text></P2para></P2><P2 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2006/223/regulation/3/5" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2006/223/regulation/3/5" id="regulation-3-5"><Pnumber><CommentaryRef Ref="key-a11"/>5</Pnumber><P2para><Text>. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .</Text></P2para></P2></P1para></P1></P1group></Part></Body></Secondary><Commentaries><Commentary id="key-a6" Type="F"><Para><Text>Reg. 3(2)(d) and preceding word inserted (16.8.2007) by <Citation URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2007/2150" id="c411i20z4-00007" Class="UnitedKingdomStatutoryInstrument" Year="2007" Number="2150" Title="The Child Benefit (General) (Amendment) Regulations 2007">The Child Benefit (General) (Amendment) Regulations 2007 (S.I. 2007/2150)</Citation>, <CitationSubRef CitationRef="c411i20z4-00007" id="c411i20z4-00008" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2007/2150/regulation/1" SectionRef="regulation-1">regs. 1</CitationSubRef>, <CitationSubRef CitationRef="c411i20z4-00007" id="c411i20z4-00009" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2007/2150/regulation/4/b" SectionRef="regulation-4-b" Operative="true">4(b)</CitationSubRef></Text></Para></Commentary><Commentary id="key-a5" Type="F"><Para><Text>Words in reg. 3(2)(b) substituted (16.8.2007) by <Citation URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2007/2150" id="c411i20z4-00016" Class="UnitedKingdomStatutoryInstrument" Year="2007" Number="2150" Title="The Child Benefit (General) (Amendment) Regulations 2007">The Child Benefit (General) (Amendment) Regulations 2007 (S.I. 2007/2150)</Citation>, <CitationSubRef CitationRef="c411i20z4-00016" id="c411i20z4-00017" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2007/2150/regulation/1" SectionRef="regulation-1">regs. 1</CitationSubRef>, <CitationSubRef CitationRef="c411i20z4-00016" id="c411i20z4-00018" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2007/2150/regulation/4/a" SectionRef="regulation-4-a" Operative="true">4(a)</CitationSubRef></Text></Para></Commentary><Commentary id="key-a10" Type="F"><Para><Text>Words in reg. 3(4) inserted (16.8.2007) by <Citation URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2007/2150" id="c411i20z4-00025" Class="UnitedKingdomStatutoryInstrument" Year="2007" Number="2150" Title="The Child Benefit (General) (Amendment) Regulations 2007">The Child Benefit (General) (Amendment) Regulations 2007 (S.I. 2007/2150)</Citation>, <CitationSubRef CitationRef="c411i20z4-00025" id="c411i20z4-00026" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2007/2150/regulation/1" SectionRef="regulation-1">regs. 1</CitationSubRef>, <CitationSubRef CitationRef="c411i20z4-00025" id="c411i20z4-00027" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2007/2150/regulation/4/c" SectionRef="regulation-4-c" Operative="true">4(c)</CitationSubRef></Text></Para></Commentary><Commentary id="key-a3" Type="F"><Para><Text>Words in reg. 3(2)(b) substituted (4.6.2014) by <Citation URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2014/1231" id="c42egpxy4-00016" Class="UnitedKingdomStatutoryInstrument" Year="2014" Number="1231" Title="The Child Benefit (General) and Child Tax Credit (Amendment) Regulations 2014">The Child Benefit (General) and Child Tax Credit (Amendment) Regulations 2014 (S.I. 2014/1231)</Citation>, <CitationSubRef CitationRef="c42egpxy4-00016" id="c42egpxy4-00017" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2014/1231/regulation/1" SectionRef="regulation-1">regs. 1</CitationSubRef>, <CitationSubRef CitationRef="c42egpxy4-00016" id="c42egpxy4-00018" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2014/1231/regulation/2/3/b" SectionRef="regulation-2-3-b" Operative="true">2(3)(b)</CitationSubRef></Text></Para></Commentary><Commentary id="key-a8" Type="F"><Para><Text>Words in reg. 3(4) substituted (4.6.2014) by <Citation URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2014/1231" id="c42egpxy4-00025" Class="UnitedKingdomStatutoryInstrument" Year="2014" Number="1231" Title="The Child Benefit (General) and Child Tax Credit (Amendment) Regulations 2014">The Child Benefit (General) and Child Tax Credit (Amendment) Regulations 2014 (S.I. 2014/1231)</Citation>, <CitationSubRef CitationRef="c42egpxy4-00025" id="c42egpxy4-00026" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2014/1231/regulation/1" SectionRef="regulation-1">regs. 1</CitationSubRef>, <CitationSubRef CitationRef="c42egpxy4-00025" id="c42egpxy4-00027" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2014/1231/regulation/2/4" SectionRef="regulation-2-4" Operative="true">2(4)</CitationSubRef></Text></Para></Commentary><Commentary id="key-a4" Type="F"><Para><Text>Words in <CitationSubRef id="cwrjspp25-00006" SectionRef="regulation-3-2-b" URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2006/223/regulation/3/2/b">reg. 3(2)(b)</CitationSubRef> omitted (1.9.2025) by virtue of <Citation URI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/uksi/2025/818" id="cwrjspp25-00007" Class="UnitedKingdomStatutoryInstrument" Year="2025" Number="818" Title="The Child Benefit (Miscellaneous Amendments) Regulations 2025">The Child Benefit (Miscellaneous Amendments) Regulations 2025 (S.I. 2025/818)</Citation>, <CitationSubRef CitationRef=